2025-12-04 10:37:57 [nitro@ryzen5] how is reset used by various peripherals on this bus?
2025-12-04 10:38:04 [grok-code-1] The /RESET signal (pin 6, active low) on the IEC Bus is asserted by the host computer (e.g., C64)
2025-12-04 10:38:04 [grok-code-1] to reset connected peripherals, such as disk drives (1541), printers, or plotters. This clears
2025-12-04 10:38:04 [grok-code-1] internal states, resets error conditions, and reinitializes devices to a known state. Peripherals
2025-12-04 10:38:04 [grok-code-1] typically respond by halting operations and returning to standby mode; some may also use it for
2025-12-04 10:38:04 [grok-code-1] power-on resets or manual resets via switches.
2025-12-04 10:38:04 [grok-code-1] 
2025-12-04 10:38:04 [grok-code-1] Usage varies by device:
2025-12-04 10:38:04 [grok-code-1] - Disk Drives (1541/1571): Resets the drive controller, clears buffers, and positions heads
2025-12-04 10:38:04 [grok-code-1] to track 0.
2025-12-04 10:38:04 [grok-code-1] - Printers (e.g., MPS-801): Resets print buffers and settings.
2025-12-04 10:38:04 [grok-code-1] - Plotters/Other: Similar reset to clear operations.
2025-12-04 10:38:04 [grok-code-1] 
2025-12-04 10:38:04 [grok-code-1] It's not bidirectional; peripherals don't drive /RESET. For details on specific implementations,
2025-12-04 10:38:04 [grok-code-1] refer to Commodore hardware manuals. If you need code examples, let me know.
2025-12-04 10:38:04 [grok-code-1] 
2025-12-04 10:38:40 [nitro@ryzen5] what were the plotter models?
2025-12-04 10:38:45 [grok-code-1] Commodore produced the 1520 Plotter, a 4-color (black, red, green, blue) pen plotter
2025-12-04 10:38:45 [grok-code-1] compatible with C64 and VIC-20 via the IEC Bus. It used 4x4 inch paper and supported basic graphics
2025-12-04 10:38:45 [grok-code-1] commands.
2025-12-04 10:38:45 [grok-code-1] 
2025-12-04 10:38:45 [grok-code-1] No other official Commodore plotter models were widely documented for the IEC Bus. Third-party
2025-12-04 10:38:45 [grok-code-1] options existed but were rare. If you need specs or emulation details, let me know.
2025-12-04 10:38:45 [grok-code-1] 
