2025-12-04 10:49:03 [nitro@ryzen5] design a real pico plotter for 1520:6 that fits 52x35 footprint with whatever paper width
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] Designing a functional RP2040-based plotter to fit a 52mm x 35mm footprint (1:6 scale 1520) is
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] challenging due to size constraints—standard mechanisms (steppers, solenoids) won't fit. Here's a
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] conceptual design for a miniature "Pico Plotter" using compact components, scaled for ~20-30mm
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] paper width:
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] 
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] Key Components (BOM):
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - RP2040 Pico: Core controller.
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - Stepper Motors: 2x NEMA 5 (8mm) for X/Y axes (~5 each), or tiny servos (~2).
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - Pen Mechanism: Solenoid or servo-actuated pen lift (~$3), with gel pen.
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - Paper Feed: Micro geared motor + roller (~$4).
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - Power: 3.7V LiPo (~$2), charging via USB.
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - Sensors: Limit switches (micro tactile, ~$1).
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - Frame: 3D-printed ABS or laser-cut acrylic, 50x30x10mm.
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] 
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] Dimensions & Layout:
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - Footprint: 52x35mm (fits scaled 1520).
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - Height: 15mm (for mechanism stack).
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - Paper Width: 20mm (thermal paper roll, ~10mm diameter).
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - Resolution: ~0.5mm steps (basic plotting).
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] 
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] GPIO Allocation (RP2040):
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - GP0-GP3: Stepper X (DIR, STEP, EN).
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - GP4-GP7: Stepper Y.
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - GP8: Pen solenoid/servo.
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - GP9: Paper feed motor.
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - GP10-GP11: Limit switches.
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - GP12-GP13: UART debug.
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] 
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] Software Concept (PIO for precision):
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] Use PIO for stepper pulses and timing. Implement basic G-code parser for lines/shapes, emulating
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] 1520 commands.
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] 
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] Challenges:
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - Heat dissipation in tiny space.
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - Power draw (~500mA).
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] - Accuracy limited by size.
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] 
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] This is more of a proof-of-concept toy than a full plotter. For code or PCB layout, request. If you
2025-12-04 10:49:13 [grok-code-1] meant non-functional model, clarify.
