2025-12-04 10:56:56 [nitro@ryzen5] for pens? or should we look at a thermal tip pen?
2025-12-04 10:57:02 [grok-code-1] For thermal paper, a physical pen won't work (it needs heat activation). Switch to a thermal
2025-12-04 10:57:02 [grok-code-1] print head (e.g., from a 58mm receipt printer module) for dot-matrix "plotting"—it's compact,
2025-12-04 10:57:02 [grok-code-1] RP2040-compatible via serial/UART, and prints directly on thermal paper without ink.
2025-12-04 10:57:02 [grok-code-1] 
2025-12-04 10:57:02 [grok-code-1] - Pros: No moving pen, higher resolution (~203 DPI), simple integration.
2025-12-04 10:57:02 [grok-code-1] - Cons: Monochrome only, requires heat sink.
2025-12-04 10:57:02 [grok-code-1] - BOM Update: Replace servo/pen with thermal head (~$10-20) and driver circuit.
2025-12-04 10:57:02 [grok-code-1] 
