2025-12-04 14:23:51 [grok-code-1] that's ~3.2 million pixels/second × 16 bits = ~51.2 Mbps, well within USB 2.0 high-speed limits
2025-12-04 14:23:51 [grok-code-1] (480 Mbps) or even full-speed (12 Mbps) if optimized. It allows offloading processing/formatting to
2025-12-04 14:23:51 [grok-code-1] the second Pico for smoother output. If you're streaming full C64 color (not just luma), that fits
2025-12-04 14:23:51 [grok-code-1] perfectly—need code snippets for USB bulk transfer or PIO tweaks?
