2025-12-04 16:19:11 [gemini-3-pro] • VIC-1904: This was Slot (a slot machine simulation).
2025-12-04 16:19:11 [gemini-3-pro] • 1928-1930:
2025-12-04 16:19:11 [gemini-3-pro]     *   VIC-1928: Home Babysitter (1982) – A utility/game guide.
2025-12-04 16:19:11 [gemini-3-pro]     *   VIC-1929: Personal Finance (1982) – A budgeting utility (often excluded
2025-12-04 16:19:11 [gemini-3-pro] from game lists, but fills the numbering).
2025-12-04 16:19:11 [gemini-3-pro]     *   VIC-1930: Visible Solar System (1982) – An educational space simulation.
2025-12-04 16:19:11 [gemini-3-pro] • 1933-1936:
2025-12-04 16:19:11 [gemini-3-pro]     *   VIC-1933: Bounce (1982) – A Breakout-style game.
2025-12-04 16:19:11 [gemini-3-pro]     *   VIC-1934: Phase Ten (Unreleased/Unknown) – This slot is generally
2025-12-04 16:19:11 [gemini-3-pro] considered empty/unreleased in collector lists.
2025-12-04 16:19:11 [gemini-3-pro]     *   VIC-1935: Commodore Artist (1982) – A drawing utility (rare).
2025-12-04 16:19:11 [gemini-3-pro]     *   VIC-1936: Unreleased – No confirmed title exists for this ID.
2025-12-04 16:19:11 [gemini-3-pro] • Was VIC-1939 the last?: Not quite! VIC-1941 exists: Number Nabber / Shape
2025-12-04 16:19:11 [gemini-3-pro] Grabber (an educational game).
