2025-12-05 15:11:29 [nitro@ryzen5] what is 374 for?
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] The 74LS374 is for Project Joy - it's the output latch that drives the
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] joystick signals.
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] 74LS374 Function in Project Joy:
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] Purpose:
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] - Octal D-type flip-flop with tri-state outputs
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] - Latches 8 bits of data from RP2040
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] - Drives 2N7000 FET gates to control joystick lines
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] How it Works:
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] RP2040 GPIO (8-bit bus) → 74LS374 (latch) → 2N7000 FET → Joystick Port
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat]        ↓
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat]     Data stored
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat]     on clock edge
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] In Your Design:
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] - U6: Joy 1+2 outputs (8 FETs)
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] - U7: Joy 2+3+4 outputs (8 FETs)
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] - U8: Joy 4 + Apple outputs (8 FETs)
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] Why Latch Instead of Direct GPIO:
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] 1. Timing: Hold outputs stable while RP2040 does other tasks
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] 2. Drive Strength: 74LS374 can source/sink more current than RP2040 GPIO
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] 3. Voltage: 5V outputs for 2N7000 FET gates (RP2040 is 3.3V)
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] 4. Isolation: Protects RP2040 from joystick port issues
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] Alternative:
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] If you're short on 74LS374, you could use 74HC574 (similar) or drive FETs directly from
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] 74LVC245 (but need level shifting).
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] You have 2× 74LS374 in cart, need 1 more for the 3 latches in Project Joy.
2025-12-05 15:11:45 [deepseek-chat] 
