2025-12-05 15:23:18 [nitro@ryzen5] explain 74HC165 count
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] The 74HC165 count is for Project Joy - it's the input shift register that
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] reads joystick button states.
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 74HC165 Function in Project Joy:
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] Purpose:
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] - 8-bit parallel-in/serial-out shift register
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] - Reads 8 joystick buttons in parallel
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] - Shifts data serially to RP2040 (saves GPIO pins)
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] In Your Design:
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] You need 5× 74HC165 for:
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] - U1: Joy1 buttons (8 inputs)
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] - U2: Joy2 buttons (8 inputs)
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] - U3: Joy3 buttons (8 inputs)
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] - U4: Joy4 buttons (8 inputs)
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] - U5: Apple II buttons + AUX inputs (8 inputs)
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] Total Inputs:
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 5 chips × 8 inputs = 40 digital inputs
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] Current Status:
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] - In cart: 4× 74HC165
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] - Needed: 5 total
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] - Missing: 1 more 74HC165
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] Why 5 Chips?
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 1. 4 joystick ports × 8 buttons each = 32 inputs
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 2. Apple II (3 buttons) + AUX (5 inputs) = 8 inputs
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 3. Total: 40 inputs = 5 chips
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] Alternative if Short:
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] If you only have 4 chips, you could:
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 1. Reduce to 3 joystick ports (24 inputs)
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 2. Or reduce AUX inputs from 5 to 1
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 3. Or use direct GPIO for some inputs
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] But for the full Project Joy design, you need 5× 74HC165. You have 4 in cart - add 1
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] more to complete the set.
2025-12-05 15:23:34 [deepseek-chat] 
