2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] The 74LS374 count is also for Project Joy - it's the output latch that
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] drives joystick signals.
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] 74LS374 Function in Project Joy:
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] Purpose:
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] - Octal D-type flip-flop with tri-state outputs
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] - Latches 8 bits of data from RP2040
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] - Drives 2N7000 FET gates to control joystick lines
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] In Your Design:
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] You need 3× 74LS374 for:
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] - U6: Joy 1+2 outputs (8 FETs)
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] - U7: Joy 2+3+4 outputs (8 FETs)
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] - U8: Joy 4 + Apple outputs (8 FETs)
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] Total Outputs:
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] 3 chips × 8 outputs = 24 open-drain outputs
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] Current Status:
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] - In cart: 2× 74LS374
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] - Needed: 3 total
2025-12-05 15:25:08 [deepseek-chat] - Missing: 1 more 74LS374
