2025-12-05 15:29:57 [nitro@ryzen5] ok how about 4051 usage?
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] The 4051 (CD4051) is for Project Joy - it's the analog multiplexer that
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] reads joystick/paddle potentiometers.
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 4051 Function in Project Joy:
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Purpose:
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] - Single 8-channel analog multiplexer/demultiplexer
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] - Selects between 8 analog inputs
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] - Routes selected input to ADC pin (saves ADC channels)
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] In Your Design:
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] You need 2× 4051 for:
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] - U9: Joystick pots (4 joysticks × 2 axes = 8 inputs)
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] - U10: Apple paddles + AUX analog (4 paddles + 4 AUX = 8 inputs)
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Current Status:
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] - In cart: 2× 4051 ✓ CORRECT!
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] What Each 4051 Controls:
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] • U9 (Joystick Pots):*
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Channel 0: Joy1 X
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Channel 1: Joy1 Y
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Channel 2: Joy2 X
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Channel 3: Joy2 Y
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Channel 4: Joy3 X
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Channel 5: Joy3 Y
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Channel 6: Joy4 X
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Channel 7: Joy4 Y
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] • U10 (Apple Paddles + AUX):*
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Channel 0: PDL 0 (Apple paddle 0)
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Channel 1: PDL 1 (Apple paddle 1)
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Channel 2: PDL 2 (Apple paddle 2)
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Channel 3: PDL 3 (Apple paddle 3)
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Channel 4: AUX A0
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Channel 5: AUX A1
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Channel 6: AUX A2
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Channel 7: AUX A3
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] How It Works:
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] RP2040 GP6,7,8 (S0,S1,S2) → 4051 select pins
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] RP2040 GP26 (ADC0) ← U9 COM (reads joystick pots)
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] RP2040 GP27 (ADC1) ← U10 COM (reads paddles/AUX)
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] Why 4051 Instead of Direct ADC:
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 1. RP2040 only has 3 ADC pins (GP26,27,28)
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 2. 4051 lets you read 16 analog inputs with just 2 ADC pins
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 3. Fast switching - can scan all inputs quickly
2025-12-05 15:30:19 [deepseek-chat] 
