2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] Looking at those two LCD modules, they appear to have different communication protocols:
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] • 1. 2-inch LCD Display Module (19888):*
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] - Protocol: Standard 4-wire SPI (Serial Peripheral Interface)
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] - Typical pins: CS (Chip Select), DC (Data/Command), SCLK (Clock), MOSI (Data), RST
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] (Reset), BL (Backlight)
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] - Driver: Likely ST7789 or similar
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] - No touch capability
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] • 2. 1.28-inch Touch Display Module (19804):*
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] - Protocol: Dual interface:
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat]   - Display: 4-wire SPI for the screen
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat]   - Touch: I2C or SPI for the touch controller (likely I2C for capacitive touch)
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] - Typical pins:
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat]   - Display: CS, DC, SCLK, MOSI, RST, BL
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat]   - Touch: SDA, SCL (I2C) or additional SPI pins
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] - Driver: Display driver + touch controller (CST816S or similar)
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] • Key differences:*
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] - Touch vs Non-touch: The 1.28" has capacitive touch, requiring additional communication
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] protocol
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] - Size: 2" vs 1.28" (different resolutions but both 320x240)
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] - Interface complexity: The touch version needs both SPI for display and I2C for touch
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] input
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-05 23:57:51 [deepseek-chat] • For your projects:*
