2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] Thermal Management:
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] - 3mm air gap between PCBs for airflow
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] - Ventilation holes in top/bottom covers
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] - Low-power components (RP2040 runs cool)
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] - No heatsinks needed at 12mm height
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] Assembly Sequence:
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] 1. Solder components to bottom PCB
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] 2. Install 20-pin vertical header
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] 3. Add 3mm spacers
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] 4. Place top PCB on spacers
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] 5. Solder top PCB components
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] 6. Connect inter-board wiring
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] 7. Install top cover
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] 52×52mm Advantages:
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] - Standard PCB size (no extra cost)
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] - Perfect for 2×2 grid of Pico-sized modules
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] - Room for headers on all sides
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] - Fits standard enclosures
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] This gives you a dense but manageable internal layout that maximizes the 12mm height while
2025-12-06 00:34:31 [deepseek-chat] maintaining serviceability. The 3mm air gap is crucial for cooling and makes assembly easier.
