2025-12-06 00:46:19 [nitro@ryzen5] which side of the pico for the data bus
2025-12-06 00:46:51 [deepseek-chat] For the RP2040 Pico, the data bus (GPIO pins) are primarily on BOTH sides,
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] but here's the breakdown:
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] RP2040 Pico Pin Layout:
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] Top View (USB at top):
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] ┌─────────────────────┐
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │      USB-C          │ ← Top edge
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] ├─────────────────────┤
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │ ● ● ● ● ● ● ● ●     │ ← LEFT side (20 pins)
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │ 0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7     │    GPIO0-GPIO7 (low byte)
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │                     │
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │                     │
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │ ● ● ● ● ● ● ● ●     │ ← RIGHT side (20 pins)
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │ 8 9 10 11 12 13 14 15│    GPIO8-GPIO15 (high byte)
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │                     │
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │                     │
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │ ● ● ● ● ● ● ● ●     │ ← BOTTOM edge (8 pins)
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │ 16 17 18 19 20 21 22│    GPIO16-GPIO22 + RUN
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] └─────────────────────┘
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] For Your Cube/Board Design:
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] Option A: Data Bus on One Side (Recommended)
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] Place Pico with USB facing FRONT of cube:
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] ┌─────────────────────┐
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │       FRONT         │ ← USB port faces user
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │                     │
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │ LEFT       RIGHT    │
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │ GPIO0-7    GPIO8-15 │ ← Data bus split
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │                     │
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │       BACK          │ ← GPIO16-22 + power
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] └─────────────────────┘
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] Option B: Dedicated Bus Side
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] Rotate Pico 90°:
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] ┌─────────────────────┐
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │       TOP           │ ← USB
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │                     │
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │ LEFT    RIGHT       │
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │ (GPIO0-15)          │ ← ALL data pins on one side
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │                     │
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │       BOTTOM        │ ← Power + remaining GPIO
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] └─────────────────────┘
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] Recommended Layout for 51mm Cube:
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] Cube interior (looking at Pico placement):
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] ┌─────────────────────┐
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │       USB-C         │ ← Faces FRONT panel
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │                     │
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │ GPIO0-15  →         │ ← All data pins face RIGHT
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │                     │    (toward backplane connector)
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │                     │
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] │ Power/rest →        │ ← Faces LEFT (internal)
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] └─────────────────────┘
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] Backplane Connection Strategy:
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 20-pin connector on RIGHT side of Pico:
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] ┌─────────────────────┐
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] Pins 1-16: GPIO0-GPIO15 (16-bit data bus)
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] Pin 17: GND
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] Pin 18: 3.3V
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] Pin 19: 5V
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] Pin 20: Reserved/GPIO16
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] └─────────────────────┘
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] Why GPIO0-15 on One Side?
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 1. 16-bit bus naturally groups on GPIO0-15
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 2. Remaining GPIO (16-22) for control signals
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 3. USB faces front for accessibility
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 4. Clean routing to backplane connector
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 5. Standardized across all modules
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] For Your Modular System:
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] Every module board should have the Pico oriented the same way:
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] - USB port: Always faces "front" of cube
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] - Data bus (GPIO0-15): Always on "right" side
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] - Backplane connector: Always on "right" side
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] - Power/control: Always on "left" side
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] This creates a consistent internal architecture that makes module design predictable and
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] interconnects reliable.
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] Would you like me to draw the exact PCB layout for the first module?
2025-12-06 00:46:52 [deepseek-chat] 
