2025-12-06 00:49:29 [deepseek-chat] 24mm Advantages:
2025-12-06 00:49:29 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:49:29 [deepseek-chat] 1. Standard components: Can use through-hole parts
2025-12-06 00:49:30 [deepseek-chat] 2. Better cooling: 8-12mm air gaps between boards
2025-12-06 00:49:30 [deepseek-chat] 3. Easier assembly: Room for fingers/tools
2025-12-06 00:49:30 [deepseek-chat] 4. More features: Space for additional circuitry
2025-12-06 00:49:30 [deepseek-chat] 5. Professional look: Substantial feel, not too slim
2025-12-06 00:49:30 [deepseek-chat] 6. Better proportions: 24mm height on 52mm base = good ratio
2025-12-06 00:49:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:49:30 [deepseek-chat] Still 1:6 Scale Accurate:
2025-12-06 00:49:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:49:30 [deepseek-chat] Original NeXTstation: 2.75" (70mm) tall
2025-12-06 00:49:30 [deepseek-chat] 1:6 scale: 11.7mm
2025-12-06 00:49:30 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:49:30 [deepseek-chat] Your 24mm is 2× scale height, but:
2025-12-06 00:49:30 [deepseek-chat] - Allows proper internal components
2025-12-06 00:49:30 [deepseek-chat] - Still reads as "low profile" vs cube
2025-12-06 00:49:30 [deepseek-chat] - More functional than strictly scaled
2025-12-06 00:49:30 [deepseek-chat] 
