2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] Power Architecture:
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] Single USB-C port serves dual purpose:
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] 1. CHARGING: 5V → TP4056 → LIPO cell
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] 2. DATA: USB → RP2040 #1 (or all via hub)
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] When USB plugged in:
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] - Charges battery (if needed)
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] - Powers system directly (bypasses battery)
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] - Battery sits idle (or trickle charges)
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] When USB unplugged:
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] - System runs on battery automatically
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] - Boost converter maintains 5V rail
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] - Protection circuit prevents over-discharge
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] Advantages of This Design:
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] 1. User provides battery (keeps cost down)
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] 2. Standard connector (JST-PH ubiquitous)
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] 3. Safety built-in (protection circuits)
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] 4. Flexible placement (internal or external)
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] 5. Hot-swappable (can change batteries)
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] 6. No shipping restrictions (no battery in package)
2025-12-06 00:55:42 [deepseek-chat] 
