2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] The TS file is a compact, self-contained 16-colour GIF encoder that already works.
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] The only real “issue” is that the canvas size (404 × 284) and the offsets you feed into the GIF
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] header are hard-coded for a C64-border look, but the GIF you build only contains the 320 × 200
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] playfield.
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] If you want the file to open in viewers exactly like a C64 screenshot (i.e. the border is visible
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] and filled with the current border colour) you have to render the border pixels as well.
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] That means:
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Allocate a 404 × 284 frame buffer.
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Clear it to the current border colour each frame.
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. Blit the 320 × 200 playfield into the middle.
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 4. Pack / compress the whole 404 × 284 image.
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] Everything else (bit-packing, LZW, block splitting) is already correct.
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] Below is a drop-in replacement for the three methods that need to change.
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] No other code has to be touched.
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] // --- replace the three affected private methods --------------------------
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] #pack() {
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 	const w = this.#cw;               // 404
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 	const h = this.#ch;               // 284
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 	const out = new Uint8Array((w >> 1) * h);
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 	// 1. whole canvas → border colour
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 	const border = this.#bg;
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 	for (let i = 0; i < out.length; i++) out[i] = (border << 4) | border;
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 	// 2. copy 320×200 playfield into centre
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 	const src = this.#frame;
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 	for (let sy = 0; sy < this.#h; sy++) {
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 		const dy = this.#py + sy;
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 		for (let sx = 0; sx < this.#w; sx += 2) {
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 			const dx = this.#px + sx;
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 			const hi = src[sy * this.#w + sx];
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 			const lo = src[sy * this.#w + sx + 1];
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 			out[(dy * (w >> 1)) + (dx >> 1)] = (hi << 4) | lo;
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 		}
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 	}
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 	return out;
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] // --- keep the original compress / finish, nothing else changes ----------
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] #compress(data: Uint8Array) { /* unchanged */ }
2025-12-06 09:56:18 [kimi-k2-0905] finish() { /* unchanged */ }
