2025-12-06 10:48:27 [kimi-k2-0905] The file is a compact, self-contained GIF encoder that targets a 320×200 16-colour “C-64 style”
2025-12-06 10:48:27 [kimi-k2-0905] canvas and packs two 4-bit pixels per byte.
2025-12-06 10:48:27 [kimi-k2-0905] It writes a global colour table, Netscape looping extension, and one graphic control + image block
2025-12-06 10:48:27 [kimi-k2-0905] per frame.
2025-12-06 10:48:27 [kimi-k2-0905] LZW uses a 5-bit starting code size and grows to 12 bits.
2025-12-06 10:48:27 [kimi-k2-0905] The demo produces a 32-frame checkerboard animation.
2025-12-06 10:48:27 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-06 10:48:27 [kimi-k2-0905] No obvious bugs; the encoder will emit a valid GIF if the consumer respects the public API
2025-12-06 10:48:27 [kimi-k2-0905] (setPixel / setBorder / addFrame / finish).
