2025-12-06 11:06:02 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the fixed `gif16.ts`.
2025-12-06 11:06:02 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-06 11:06:02 [gemini-3-pro] The main issues were:
2025-12-06 11:06:02 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Pixel Packing: The `#pack` method was compressing 2 pixels into 1 byte (4-bit packed),
2025-12-06 11:06:02 [gemini-3-pro] but standard GIF LZW expects a stream of 8-bit indices (one byte per pixel) for the compressor.
2025-12-06 11:06:02 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  LZW Configuration: The compressor was configured for 4-bit codes (Clear 16), but the
2025-12-06 11:06:02 [gemini-3-pro] frame header was specifying an 8-bit minimum code size. I adjusted the frame header to `0x04` (Min
2025-12-06 11:06:02 [gemini-3-pro] Code Size 4) to match the 16-color palette logic.
2025-12-06 11:06:02 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Palette Loading: The `flatMap` logic in the default parameter was discarding the Red
2025-12-06 11:06:02 [gemini-3-pro] channel. I replaced it with a direct `Uint8Array` from the RGB data.
2025-12-06 11:06:02 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  Compressor Logic: The LZW implementation was simplified and made robust to handle code
2025-12-06 11:06:02 [gemini-3-pro] size increases and clear codes correctly.
