2025-12-06 11:12:57 [gemini-3-pro] The main issues fixed are:
2025-12-06 11:12:57 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  LZW Compression: The previous packing of 2 pixels per byte was incompatible with
2025-12-06 11:12:57 [gemini-3-pro] standard GIF LZW, which expects a stream of color indices. The `#pack` method was removed, and
2025-12-06 11:12:57 [gemini-3-pro] indices (0-15) are now compressed directly.
2025-12-06 11:12:57 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Code Size: The LZW Minimum Code Size is now correctly set to `4` (for 16 colors), and
2025-12-06 11:12:57 [gemini-3-pro] the compressor correctly handles the 5-bit start size (Clear=16, EOI=17).
2025-12-06 11:12:57 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Palette & Header: The Logical Screen Descriptor is updated to `0xF3` to correctly
2025-12-06 11:12:57 [gemini-3-pro] declare a 16-color global table, ensuring the decoder parses the 48-byte palette correctly.
2025-12-06 11:12:57 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  Compressor Logic: The LZW dictionary logic was updated to correctly handle code
2025-12-06 11:12:57 [gemini-3-pro] assignment and table clears.
