2025-12-06 11:25:00 [gemini-3-pro] The previous implementation had a few critical issues causing corruption:
2025-12-06 11:25:00 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Incorrect Pixel Packing: The `#pack` method combined two pixels into one byte. GIF LZW
2025-12-06 11:25:00 [gemini-3-pro] expects a stream of individual color indices (one byte per pixel), not packed pixels. This caused
2025-12-06 11:25:00 [gemini-3-pro] the decoder to run out of data halfway through the image.
2025-12-06 11:25:00 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  LZW Code Size Mismatch: The compressor was configured for 4-bit data (Clear Code 16),
2025-12-06 11:25:00 [gemini-3-pro] but the file header claimed an 8-bit minimum code size. This desynchronized the bit stream.
2025-12-06 11:25:00 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Palette Definition: The Global Color Table size in the Logical Screen Descriptor
2025-12-06 11:25:00 [gemini-3-pro] (`#lsd`) claimed 256 colors (`0x87`), but only 48 bytes of palette data were written, causing the
2025-12-06 11:25:00 [gemini-3-pro] decoder to interpret the following header data as colors.
2025-12-06 11:25:00 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-06 11:25:00 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the corrected, working `gif16.ts`.
