2025-12-07 09:19:19 [nitro@ryzen5] what is commodore c64dtv
2025-12-07 09:19:31 [gemini-3-pro] The Commodore 64 Direct-to-TV (C64DTV) is a single-unit plug-and-play console released in 2004.
2025-12-07 09:19:31 [gemini-3-pro] Housed entirely inside a joystick controller, it connects directly to a television via composite
2025-12-07 09:19:31 [gemini-3-pro] cables and comes with 30 built-in games.
2025-12-07 09:19:31 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:19:31 [gemini-3-pro] It was designed by Jeri Ellsworth and is distinct from many other plug-and-play devices because it
2025-12-07 09:19:31 [gemini-3-pro] uses a custom ASIC to provide hardware-level simulation of the C64, rather than software emulation.
2025-12-07 09:19:31 [gemini-3-pro] The device is highly regarded in the modding community because the internal circuit board contains
2025-12-07 09:19:31 [gemini-3-pro] exposed solder points that allow users to attach a PS/2 keyboard and IEC disk drives, effectively
2025-12-07 09:19:31 [gemini-3-pro] converting the joystick into a fully functional Commodore 64 computer.
2025-12-07 09:19:31 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:21:12 [nitro@ryzen5] commodore basic commands clear screen, poke color mem
2025-12-07 09:21:25 [gemini-3-pro] The Commodore 64 DTV (Direct-to-TV) is a plug-and-play console contained entirely within a
2025-12-07 09:21:25 [gemini-3-pro] joystick. Released in 2004 and designed by Jeri Ellsworth, it features a single-chip implementation
2025-12-07 09:21:25 [gemini-3-pro] of the C64 hardware and includes 30 built-in games.
2025-12-07 09:21:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:21:25 [gemini-3-pro] Here are the BASIC commands you requested:
2025-12-07 09:21:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:21:25 [gemini-3-pro] • Clear Screen*
2025-12-07 09:21:25 [gemini-3-pro] The standard method to clear the screen programmatically is to print the control character 147.
2025-12-07 09:21:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:21:25 [gemini-3-pro] PRINT CHR$(147)
2025-12-07 09:21:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:21:26 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:21:26 [gemini-3-pro] • POKE Color Memory*
2025-12-07 09:21:26 [gemini-3-pro] Color RAM starts at address 55296 ($D800). To change the color of a specific character cell, POKE
2025-12-07 09:21:26 [gemini-3-pro] the address with a value between 0 and 15.
2025-12-07 09:21:26 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:21:26 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:21:26 [gemini-3-pro] REM Sets the top-left character color to White (1)
2025-12-07 09:21:26 [gemini-3-pro] POKE 55296, 1
2025-12-07 09:21:26 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:21:26 [gemini-3-pro] 
