2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] The Commodore 64 DTV (Direct-to-TV) is a dedicated console contained entirely within a
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] joystick, released in 2004. Designed by Jeri Ellsworth, it features a single-chip ASIC
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] implementation of the C64 hardware and comes with 30 built-in games. It is known for being highly
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] moddable.
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] Here are the BASIC commands you requested for the C64 architecture.
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] • Clear Screen*
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] To clear the screen programmatically:
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] PRINT CHR$(147)
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] • POKE Character and Color*
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] The C64 uses a memory map where Screen RAM (text) and Color RAM are separate.
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] • Screen RAM start: 1024
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] • Color RAM start: 55296
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] • Solid Block Character: 160
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:23:28 [gemini-3-pro] To place a solid white block in the top-left corner:
