2025-12-07 09:29:31 [nitro@ryzen5] what happens whan i type save "plot" in vice?
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] Here are the answers regarding the Commodore C64 DTV and the specific BASIC commands you requested.
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] • The Commodore C64 DTV*
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] The C64 DTV (Direct-to-TV) is a plug-and-play console housed entirely inside a joystick, released
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] in 2004. Designed by Jeri Ellsworth, it features a "C64-on-a-chip" ASIC, includes 30 built-in
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] games, and is well-known for being easily hackable to attach keyboards and floppy drives.
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] • BASIC Commands*
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] • Clear Screen:
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro]     `PRINT CHR$(147)`
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] • Poke Color Memory:
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro]     Color memory begins at address 55296 ($D800). To set the top-left character to white (color
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] code 1):
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro]     `POKE 55296, 1`
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] • Poke Solid Block:
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro]     Screen memory begins at address 1024 ($0400). To place a solid block (reverse space, character
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] code 160) in the top-left corner:
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro]     `POKE 1024, 160`
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] • Behavior of `SAVE "PLOT"` in VICE*
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] When you omit the device number (e.g., `,8`), the C64 defaults to Device 1 (Datasette/Tape).
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  VICE Interception: The emulator traps the tape motor signal.
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Action: If a tape image is attached, it records to that image. If no image is attached,
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] VICE typically opens a file dialog on your host operating system, allowing you to save the program
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] as a `.tap` (tape image) or `.prg` file.
2025-12-07 09:29:53 [gemini-3-pro] 
