2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] Here are the answers regarding the Commodore 64 and VICE emulator.
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] • Commodore C64DTV*
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] The C64 Direct-to-TV (C64DTV) is a plug-and-play console contained entirely within a joystick,
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] released in 2004. Designed by Jeri Ellsworth, it features a single-chip implementation of the C64
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] hardware. It includes 30 built-in games and is known for being easily modifiable (hackable) to add
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] keyboard, IEC disk drive, and joystick ports.
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] • BASIC Commands*
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] • Clear Screen: `PRINT CHR$(147)`
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] • POKE Color Memory: Color RAM starts at address 55296 ($D800). To change the color of the
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] top-left character:
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro]     `POKE 55296, 1` (Where 1 is the color code, usually white).
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] • POKE Solid Block: The solid block character is code 160. Screen memory starts at 1024
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] ($0400). To place a block at the top-left:
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro]     `POKE 1024, 160`
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] • VICE Emulator Questions*
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] • `SAVE "PLOT"`: When you type this in VICE, the emulator attempts to save the program
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro] currently in memory to the active device (usually Device 8).
2025-12-07 09:30:57 [gemini-3-pro]     *   If a disk image (.d64) is attached, the file is written inside that image.
