2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] Here are the answers regarding the C64 DTV, BASIC commands, and VICE emulation files.
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] • Commodore C64 DTV*
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] The C64 Direct-to-TV (DTV) is a single-chip implementation of the Commodore 64 computer housed
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] entirely inside a joystick controller. Released in 2004, it connects directly to a television and
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] includes built-in games. It is known for being highly hackable by hardware enthusiasts.
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] • Commodore BASIC Commands*
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] • Clear Screen:
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro]     `PRINT CHR$(147)`
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] • POKE Solid Block (Screen RAM):
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro]     The screen memory typically starts at 1024. The solid block character code is 160.
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro]     `POKE 1024, 160` (Puts a block in the top-left corner).
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] • POKE Color (Color RAM):
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro]     Color memory typically starts at 55296 ($D800).
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro]     `POKE 55296, 1` (Sets the top-left character color to White).
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] • SAVE "PLOT" in VICE*
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] By default, the `SAVE` command without a device number targets Device 1 (Datasette/Tape). In the
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] VICE emulator, this usually triggers a dialog box prompting you to create or attach a Tape Image
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] file (`.tap` or `.t64`) so the emulator has a virtual place to write the data.
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] • chargen-901225-01.bin*
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, this file is the Character ROM. Specifically, `chargen-901225-01.bin` is the 4KB binary dump
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] of the original Commodore 64 character generator hardware. VICE uses this file to emulate how the
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] C64 draws text and graphical symbols on the screen.
2025-12-07 09:31:55 [gemini-3-pro] 
