2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] 3. CBM BASIC Syntax Error
2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, this is standard behavior for CBM BASIC V2.
2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] • The Error:*
2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] `IF X=40 X=0` is invalid. You must use the keyword `THEN` before a variable assignment.
2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] • Correct Syntax:*
2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] IF X=40 THEN X=0:Y=Y+8
2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] • How the Colon Works in IF statements:*
2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] In CBM BASIC, if the condition is false, the interpreter skips the rest of the line.
2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] • If `X` is 40: It executes `X=0` AND `Y=Y+8`.
2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] • If `X` is NOT 40: It ignores `X=0` AND ignores `Y=Y+8`, moving immediately to the next line
2025-12-07 10:01:04 [gemini-3-pro] number.
