2025-12-07 10:31:20 [nitro@ryzen5] on c64 poke scroll y and window size bits
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] The register controlling vertical scrolling and window size is 53265 (`$D011`).
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Bit Breakdown:*
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Bit 3 (RSEL): Controls the window height.
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro]     *   1 = 25 rows (Default).
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro]     *   0 = 24 rows (Crops top and bottom borders).
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Bits 0–2 (YSCROLL): Controls the vertical smooth scroll position (values 0–7).
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] To change these settings without disrupting other graphics modes (like screen blanking or bitmap
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] mode), you should mask the current value.
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Examples:*
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] To set 24 rows:
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] `POKE 53265, PEEK(53265) AND 247`
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] To set 25 rows:
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] `POKE 53265, PEEK(53265) OR 8`
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] To set scroll value (where X is 0 to 7):
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] `POKE 53265, (PEEK(53265) AND 248) OR X`
2025-12-07 10:31:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:32:06 [nitro@ryzen5] list of all bits in that reg
2025-12-07 10:32:22 [gemini-3-pro] The register controlling Vertical Scrolling and Window Size (Row Select) on the Commodore 64 is
2025-12-07 10:32:22 [gemini-3-pro] $D011 (Decimal: 53265).
2025-12-07 10:32:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:32:22 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the breakdown of all bits in this register:
2025-12-07 10:32:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:32:22 [gemini-3-pro] • Bit 7: RST8 (Raster Line Bit 8 - Used with $D012 for raster positions > 255)
2025-12-07 10:32:22 [gemini-3-pro] • Bit 6: ECM (Extended Background Color Mode Enable)
2025-12-07 10:32:22 [gemini-3-pro] • Bit 5: BMM (Bitmap Mode Enable)
2025-12-07 10:32:22 [gemini-3-pro] • Bit 4: DEN (Display Enable / Screen Blanking)
2025-12-07 10:32:22 [gemini-3-pro] • Bit 3: RSEL (Row Select / Window Size)
2025-12-07 10:32:22 [gemini-3-pro]     *   0 = 24 Rows (Shrinks border inward)
2025-12-07 10:32:22 [gemini-3-pro]     *   1 = 25 Rows (Default)
2025-12-07 10:32:22 [gemini-3-pro] • Bits 0-2: YSCROLL (Vertical Smooth Scroll)
2025-12-07 10:32:22 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Values 0 to 7 shift the screen vertically by pixels.
2025-12-07 10:32:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:38:25 [nitro@ryzen5] can commodore hex in and out?
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] The register responsible for vertical scrolling and window height (row select) on the Commodore 64
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] is $D011 (Decimal 53265), often called VIC-II Control Register 1.
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the breakdown of the bits in this register:
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Bit 7 (RST8): Raster Line (Most Significant Bit). Combined with register $D012 to track
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] the current scanline.
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Bit 6 (ECM): Extended Color Mode Enable.
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Bit 5 (BMM): Bitmap Mode Enable.
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Bit 4 (DEN): Display Enable (0 = Screen Off/Blank, 1 = Screen On).
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Bit 3 (RSEL): Row Select / Screen Height.
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro]     *   0 = 24 Rows (Shrinks border inward).
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro]     *   1 = 25 Rows (Standard).
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Bits 0-2 (YSCROLL): Vertical Smooth Scroll.
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Values 0 to 7 shift the screen vertically by pixels.
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Regarding Hexadecimal in BASIC V2:*
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] No, the standard C64 BASIC V2 does not support hexadecimal input (e.g., `$D011`) or output
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] natively. You must use decimal numbers for `POKE` and `PEEK` commands. Hexadecimal support requires
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] a Machine Language Monitor cartridge or specific software extensions.
2025-12-07 10:38:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:40:19 [nitro@ryzen5] peek(vic1) is 27 always
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] The register for Y-scroll and window height (rows) is VIC Control Register 1.
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] • Address:* 53265 ($D011)
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] Bit Breakdown for 53265 ($D011)
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] ╭─────────┬────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] │  Bit    │  Name  │  Function                                             │
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] ├─────────┼────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] │  :---   │  :---  │  :---                                                 │
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] │  **7**  │  RST8  │  Raster Line (Most Significant Bit)                   │
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] │  **6**  │  ECM   │  Extended Background Color Mode (1 = On)              │
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] │  **5**  │  BMM   │  Bitmap Mode (1 = Enable)                             │
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] │  **4**  │  DEN   │  Screen Display Enable (0 = Blank, 1 = On)            │
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] │  **3**  │  RSEL  │  Row Select / Window Size (0 = 24 rows, 1 = 25 rows)  │
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] │  **2**  │  YSCL  │  Vertical Smooth Scroll (4)                           │
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] │  **1**  │  YSCL  │  Vertical Smooth Scroll (2)                           │
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] │  **0**  │  YSCL  │  Vertical Smooth Scroll (1)                           │
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] ╰─────────┴────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] • Bits 0-2 combine to form the scroll value (0-7).*
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] Hex Input/Output
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] • No.* Standard Commodore 64 BASIC V2 does not support hexadecimal literals (like `D011`)
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] or output natively. You must convert hex to decimal for `PEEK` and `POKE` commands (e.g., D011 =
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] 53265).
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] Regarding PEEK being 27
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] The value 27 (Hex `$1B`, Binary `%00011011`) is the standard power-on default for this
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] register.
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] • Bit 4 (1): Screen On.
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] • Bit 3 (1): 25 Rows (Standard window size).
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] • Bits 0-2 (3): Default vertical scroll position.
2025-12-07 10:40:39 [gemini-3-pro] 
