2025-12-07 17:08:30 [nitro@ryzen5] was PET 2001 same as CBM 4016
2025-12-07 17:08:44 [gemini-3-pro] No, they are different models representing different generations of Commodore's hardware, though
2025-12-07 17:08:44 [gemini-3-pro] they share the same MOS 6502 processor architecture.
2025-12-07 17:08:44 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 17:08:44 [gemini-3-pro] • PET 2001 (Released 1977)*
2025-12-07 17:08:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Display: 9-inch built-in monitor.
2025-12-07 17:08:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Storage: Built-in cassette tape drive.
2025-12-07 17:08:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Keyboard: typically a small calculator-style "chicklet" keyboard.
2025-12-07 17:08:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Software: BASIC 1.0.
2025-12-07 17:08:44 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-07 17:08:44 [gemini-3-pro] • CBM 4016 (Released c. 1980)*
2025-12-07 17:08:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Display: Larger 12-inch green phosphor monitor.
2025-12-07 17:08:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Storage: No internal cassette drive; relied on external units.
2025-12-07 17:08:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Keyboard: Full-stroke professional typewriter-style keyboard.
2025-12-07 17:08:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Software: Upgraded BASIC 4.0.
2025-12-07 17:08:44 [gemini-3-pro] 
