2025-12-08 09:16:36 [nitro@ryzen5] did acorn acornsoft do manuals and books?
2025-12-08 09:16:43 [kimi-k2-0905] Acornsoft itself only bundled slim “User Guide” ring-bound leaflets with each game; longer-form
2025-12-08 09:16:43 [kimi-k2-0905] books were subcontracted to third-party publishers (e.g. Dabs Press, Adder, Dutton) or appeared in
2025-12-08 09:16:43 [kimi-k2-0905] Acorn User / Beebug compilations. So nothing under the Acornsoft imprint beyond the in-box leaflet.
2025-12-08 09:16:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 09:17:16 [nitro@ryzen5] reference material for the archimedes range?
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] Acorn produced a small shelf of first-party technical manuals; most were ring-bound A4 and sold
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] through Acorn Dealer parts counters rather than high-street software shops.  The ones that turn up
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] for the Archimedes range are:
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] - “Archimedes 300/400 Series User Guide” (1987, part 0476,075) – system overview, RISC OS 1
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] desktop, connector pin-outs.
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] - “Archimedes 300/400 Series Service Manual” (1988, part 0476,076) – board layouts, power-supply
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] schematics, DRAM upgrade procedure, VIDC/IOC register map.
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] - “ARM Data Manual” (Acorn-printed, 1987, ARM DDI 0002) – ARM2 instruction set, cycle timings,
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] coprocessor interface.
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] - “RISC OS Programmer’s Reference Manual” (1989, part 0476,078) – SWI list, VIDC/IOMD memory-mapped
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] registers, sound DMA, sprite format.
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] - “RISC OS Style Guide” (1989) – WIMP red-book UI conventions, toolbox templates, drag-and-drop
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] protocol.
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] - “Archimedes Welcome Disk & Tutorial” (1987) – 800 kB disc + 40-page booklet, shipped with every
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] A3xx.
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] All were available as separate SKUs from Acorn Parts (£15–£35); none carried an “Acornsoft” logo.
2025-12-08 09:17:39 [kimi-k2-0905] 
