2025-12-08 10:21:50 [nitro@ryzen5] how do i do custom char map?
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] You're right to double-check—setting `CHAREN` low (bit 1 of `01`) only enables the
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] character generator ROM at `D000`.
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] To actually use your own 2 kB character set you must:
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Turn the ROM off (so RAM appears at `$D000`).
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Copy your 2 kB shape table to `2000`–`27FF` (or any 2 kB-aligned RAM block).
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. Tell VIC-II to fetch character data from that bank instead of ROM.
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] Minimal C64 BASIC example (assumes 4 kB VIC bank 0, `0000`–`3FFF`):
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 10 REM ----- CUSTOM CHAR SET -----
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 20 REM bank 0, RAM at $2000
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 30 POKE 56334,PEEK(56334)AND254:REM STOP CI IRQ
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 40 POKE 1,PEEK(1)AND251:REM ROM OFF
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 50 FOR A=0 TO 2047:POKE 8192+A,PEEK(53248+A):NEXT:REM COPY ROM->RAM
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 60 REM edit chars at 8192+ now
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 70 POKE 53272,(PEEK(53272)AND240)OR8:REM CHBASE=$2000
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 80 POKE 56334,PEEK(56334)OR1:REM RESTORE IRQ
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] Lines 30–40 disable the kernal/charset ROMs; line 50 copies the original shapes to RAM so you can
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] safely edit them.
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] After running, characters live at 8192–10239; change those bytes to redefine glyphs.
2025-12-08 10:22:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 
