2025-12-08 10:38:32 [nitro@ryzen5] is this clear?
2025-12-08 10:38:33 [nitro@ryzen5] # VIC-II Registers0xd018,53272,vid:4|char:3|pad:1
2025-12-08 10:38:42 [kimi-k2-0905] Not quite—`$D018` is simpler:
2025-12-08 10:38:42 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 10:38:42 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 10:38:42 [kimi-k2-0905] $D018  53272  CHBAS
2025-12-08 10:38:42 [kimi-k2-0905]        bits 7-4 : video matrix base (screen) >> 10
2025-12-08 10:38:42 [kimi-k2-0905]        bits 3-1 : character data base >> 10
2025-12-08 10:38:42 [kimi-k2-0905]        bit 0    : unused
2025-12-08 10:38:42 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 10:38:42 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 10:38:42 [kimi-k2-0905] So “vid:4 | char:3 | pad:1” is misleading; bit 0 is not a pad, it’s simply ignored.
2025-12-08 10:38:42 [kimi-k2-0905] 
