2025-12-08 10:43:34 [nitro@ryzen5] 9 bits in 1 byte????
2025-12-08 10:43:42 [kimi-k2-0905] No—bit 7 (`RST8`) is the ninth raster bit; the low 3 bits are the Y-scroll (0-7).
2025-12-08 10:43:42 [kimi-k2-0905] So the byte is:
2025-12-08 10:43:42 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 10:43:42 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 10:43:42 [kimi-k2-0905] bit 7  RST8        (MSB of 9-bit raster compare)
2025-12-08 10:43:42 [kimi-k2-0905] bit 6  yscroll2
2025-12-08 10:43:42 [kimi-k2-0905] bit 5  yscroll1
2025-12-08 10:43:42 [kimi-k2-0905] bit 4  yscroll0
2025-12-08 10:43:42 [kimi-k2-0905] bit 3  24row
2025-12-08 10:43:42 [kimi-k2-0905] bit 2  blank
2025-12-08 10:43:42 [kimi-k2-0905] bit 1  ─ (unused for scroll)
2025-12-08 10:43:42 [kimi-k2-0905] bit 0  ─ (unused for scroll)
2025-12-08 10:43:42 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 10:43:42 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 10:43:42 [kimi-k2-0905] only three y-scroll bits, not two separate groups.
2025-12-08 10:43:42 [kimi-k2-0905] 
