2025-12-08 11:01:48 [nitro@ryzen5] static is ok in typescript?
2025-12-08 11:01:49 [nitro@ryzen5] class VIC {	static MSBX = 0xD010; // 53264	static CRLC = 0xD011; // 53265	static RASTER = 0xD012; // 53266	static LPX = 0xD013; // 53267	static LPY = 0xD014; // 53268	static ENAM = 0xD015; // 53269	static XSCROLL = 0xD016; // 53270	static YEXP = 0xD017; // 53271	static CHBAS = 0xD018; // 53272	static VICIRQ = 0xD019; // 53273	static VICMASK = 0xD01A; // 53274	static SPRI = 0xD01B; // 53275	static MCM = 0xD01C; // 53276	static XEXP = 0xD01D; // 53277	static SSCOL = 0xD01E; // 53278	static SBCOL = 0xD01F; // 53279	static EXBGCOL = 0xD020; // 53280	static BGCOL0 = 0xD021; // 53281	static BGCOL1 = 0xD022; // 53282	static BGCOL2 = 0xD023; // 53283	static BGCOL3 = 0xD024; // 53284};
2025-12-08 11:01:54 [kimi-k2-0905] Yes—`static` is fine in TypeScript.
2025-12-08 11:01:54 [kimi-k2-0905] (If you prefer stricter immutability you can add `readonly`, but the above compiles cleanly.)
2025-12-08 11:01:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
