2025-12-08 17:18:12 [nitro@ryzen5] is this code ok for 6510 c64?
2025-12-08 17:18:13 [nitro@ryzen5] start   ldx #0loop    lda message,x        beq done        jsr $ffd2        inx        bne loopdone    rtsmessage !pet "hello world!",13,0
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] It’s valid 6510 source, but you can’t assemble it “as-is” with any C-64 assembler I know because
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] the mnemonics and the !pet directive are in two different syntaxes.
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] - Turbo-Assembler (and most cross-assemblers that grew out of it) wants .text or
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] .byte instead of !pet.
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] - 64tass accepts .text or "hello world!",13,0 directly after .byte.
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] So pick one style and stay with it:
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] Turbo-Assembler / ACME style
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 		* = $0801           ; BASIC start-up header if you want
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 		.word ss, 2064
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] ss		.word 0
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] start		ldx #0
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] loop		lda message,x
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 		beq done
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 		jsr $ffd2           ; CHROUT
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 		inx
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 		bne loop
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] done		rts
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] message		.text "HELLO WORLD!",13,0
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 64tass style
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 		* = $0801
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 		.word ss, 2064
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] ss		.word 0
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] start		ldx #0
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] loop		lda message,x
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 		beq done
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 		jsr $ffd2
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 		inx
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 		bne loop
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] done		rts
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] message		.byte "HELLO WORLD!",13,0
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-08 17:18:49 [kimi-k2-0905] Either version assembles to pure 6510 code and runs on every C-64.
