2025-12-08 17:27:57 [nitro@ryzen5] what is 13?
2025-12-08 17:27:58 [nitro@ryzen5] message .byte	"hello stub",13,0
2025-12-08 17:28:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 13 is PETSCII / ASCII carriage-return (`\r`).
2025-12-08 17:28:03 [kimi-k2-0905] When you send it to the KERNAL CHROUT routine (`$FFD2`) it moves the cursor to the start of the
2025-12-08 17:28:03 [kimi-k2-0905] next line—i.e. it performs a newline on the C-64 screen.
2025-12-08 17:28:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
