2025-12-09 07:39:44 [nitro@ryzen5] the 6510 specs
2025-12-09 07:39:55 [kimi-k2-0905] 6510 at a glance
2025-12-09 07:39:55 [kimi-k2-0905] - Core: 6502-compatible, NMOS, 8-bit data, 16-bit address
2025-12-09 07:39:55 [kimi-k2-0905] - Max clock: 0.985 MHz (PAL C-64) or 1.023 MHz (NTSC C-64)
2025-12-09 07:39:55 [kimi-k2-0905] - Package: 40-pin DIP
2025-12-09 07:39:55 [kimi-k2-0905] - Supply: 5 V
2025-12-09 07:39:55 [kimi-k2-0905] - Added feature: 6-bit bi-directional I/O port (pins 36-39 plus P0-P5) mapped at address 0000
2025-12-09 07:39:55 [kimi-k2-0905] (data) and 0001 (direction register); used for cassette motor, datasette sense, memory-bank select
2025-12-09 07:39:55 [kimi-k2-0905] on the 64
2025-12-09 07:39:55 [kimi-k2-0905] - Pins: standard 6502 set (RDY, IRQ, NMI, SO, RES, Φ2, R/W, A0-A15, D0-D7) plus the 6 extra I/O
2025-12-09 07:39:55 [kimi-k2-0905] lines
2025-12-09 07:39:55 [kimi-k2-0905] - No extra instructions beyond the 6502 set
2025-12-09 07:39:55 [kimi-k2-0905] - Introduced: 1983 to drop external glue logic in the C-64; functionally a 6502 with a built-in
2025-12-09 07:39:55 [kimi-k2-0905] GPIO latch
2025-12-09 07:39:55 [kimi-k2-0905] 
