2025-12-09 08:23:16 [kimi-k2-0905] A few practical gaps you could drop in next without disturbing the existing structure:
2025-12-09 08:23:16 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-09 08:23:16 [kimi-k2-0905] - interrupts – vector table (FFFA–FFFF) and IRQ/NMI/BRK dispatch behaviour
2025-12-09 08:23:16 [kimi-k2-0905] - charset – the 2 kB PETSCII ROM at F000-F7FF (or 8000-87FF on newer boards) and how the CRTC
2025-12-09 08:23:16 [kimi-k2-0905] indexes it
2025-12-09 08:23:16 [kimi-k2-0905] - CRTC – 6545 register map, cursor/blink, screen geometry, address skew
2025-12-09 08:23:16 [kimi-k2-0905] - keyboard matrix – row/column scan table that CIA1 reads
2025-12-09 08:23:16 [kimi-k2-0905] - cassette – motor relay line, sense, data in/out, jump-table vectors
2025-12-09 08:23:16 [kimi-k2-0905] - expansion – 44-pin IEEE-488 pin-out, ROM/RAM banking via $E84x decode
2025-12-09 08:23:16 [kimi-k2-0905] - timing – 1 MHz phi2, V-blank vs CRTC raster, nominal 60 Hz / 50 Hz frame rates
2025-12-09 08:23:16 [kimi-k2-0905] - power-on reset – ROM checksum, RAM test pattern, default BASIC pointers
2025-12-09 08:23:16 [kimi-k2-0905] - BASIC cold/warm start vectors – A000, E453, $E387 and how RESET re-links them
2025-12-09 08:23:16 [kimi-k2-0905] - error messages – token values 00–39 and the jump table that prints them
2025-12-09 08:23:16 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-09 08:23:16 [kimi-k2-0905] Add each as a top-level key so the file stays a single self-contained spec.
2025-12-09 08:23:16 [kimi-k2-0905] 
