2025-12-09 10:13:40 [nitro@ryzen5] can i relax "" to use <> search rules mayube
2025-12-09 10:13:43 [deepseek-chat] Yes, change:
2025-12-09 10:13:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:13:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:13:43 [deepseek-chat] #include "vice.h"
2025-12-09 10:13:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:13:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:13:43 [deepseek-chat] to:
2025-12-09 10:13:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:13:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:13:43 [deepseek-chat] #include <vice.h>
2025-12-09 10:13:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:13:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:13:43 [deepseek-chat] The `<>` will search CMake's include directories first, while `""` typically searches the current
2025-12-09 10:13:43 [deepseek-chat] file's directory first.
2025-12-09 10:13:43 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:13:53 [nitro@ryzen5] change compiler behavior?
2025-12-09 10:13:57 [deepseek-chat] You can change compiler flags in CMake:
2025-12-09 10:13:57 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:13:57 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:13:57 [deepseek-chat] # For all targets
2025-12-09 10:13:57 [deepseek-chat] set(CMAKE_C_FLAGS "${CMAKE_C_FLAGS} -I./vice-3.9/src")
2025-12-09 10:13:57 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:13:57 [deepseek-chat] # Or for specific target
2025-12-09 10:13:57 [deepseek-chat] target_include_directories(your_target PRIVATE "./vice-3.9/src")
2025-12-09 10:13:57 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:13:57 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:13:57 [deepseek-chat] The `-I` flag adds to the compiler's search path directly.
2025-12-09 10:13:57 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:14:33 [nitro@ryzen5] no for the <> vs "" include rules
2025-12-09 10:14:37 [deepseek-chat] The `<>` vs `""` rules are compiler-specific, not CMake-controlled. They're defined by the C
2025-12-09 10:14:37 [deepseek-chat] standard:
2025-12-09 10:14:37 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:14:37 [deepseek-chat] - `""`: Searches current directory first, then system paths
2025-12-09 10:14:37 [deepseek-chat] - `<>`: Searches system paths only
2025-12-09 10:14:37 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-09 10:14:37 [deepseek-chat] You can't change this behavior through CMake. Use `-I` flags to add directories to the search path
2025-12-09 10:14:37 [deepseek-chat] for both styles.
2025-12-09 10:14:37 [deepseek-chat] 
