2025-12-09 13:20:25 [gemini-3-pro] What is POS?
2025-12-09 13:20:25 [gemini-3-pro] • `POS` returns the horizontal* cursor position (column number), not the vertical
2025-12-09 13:20:25 [gemini-3-pro] position.
2025-12-09 13:20:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-09 13:20:25 [gemini-3-pro] • It returns a value from 0 to 39.
2025-12-09 13:20:25 [gemini-3-pro] • It requires a dummy argument (usually 0).
2025-12-09 13:20:25 [gemini-3-pro] • Example: `PRINT POS(0)` prints the current column of the cursor.
2025-12-09 13:20:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-09 13:20:25 [gemini-3-pro] To get the vertical row, you must read the memory address 214: `PEEK(214)`.
2025-12-09 13:20:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
