2025-12-09 13:27:55 [gemini-3-pro] • What is POS?*
2025-12-09 13:27:55 [gemini-3-pro] `POS(X)` returns the horizontal cursor position (column number 0–39). The dummy argument
2025-12-09 13:27:55 [gemini-3-pro] `X` is required but ignored.
2025-12-09 13:27:55 [gemini-3-pro] • Vertical position: There is no native token for this. It is retrieved by reading a memory
2025-12-09 13:27:55 [gemini-3-pro] address: `PEEK(214)`.
2025-12-09 13:27:55 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-09 13:27:55 [gemini-3-pro] • What is DEF?*
2025-12-09 13:27:55 [gemini-3-pro] `DEF` defines a user-defined function. It must be paired with `FN` (Function).
