2025-12-09 14:07:44 [kimi-k2-0905] (it’s optional and off by default).
2025-12-09 14:07:44 [kimi-k2-0905] Either:
2025-12-09 14:07:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-09 14:07:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Grab a nightly or self-compile with
2025-12-09 14:07:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    `--enable-rs232userip`
2025-12-09 14:07:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    in the configure line, or
2025-12-09 14:07:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-09 14:07:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Use the file or real-COM backend that’s already there:
2025-12-09 14:07:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    `-rs232userfile c:\temp\c64.log`
2025-12-09 14:07:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    `-rs232userdev com3`
2025-12-09 14:07:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-09 14:09:44 [nitro@ryzen5] nope
2025-12-09 14:09:45 [nitro@ryzen5] C:\nitrologic\dsptool>C:\nitrologic\SDL2VICE-3.9-win64-r45883\x64sc.exe -rs232userfile C:\nitrologic\c64.log Detecting DLL based HardSID boards.Cannot open hardsid.dll.LoadLibrary WPCAP.DLL failed!EthernetARCH:  LoadLibrary WPCAP.DLL failed!Detecting PCI CatWeasel boards.No PCI CatWeasel found.Reading configuration file `C:\Users\nitro\AppData\Roaming\vice\sdl-vice.ini'.Unknown option '-rs232userfile'.Error parsing command-line options, bailing out. For help use '-help'
2025-12-09 14:09:52 [kimi-k2-0905] That 3.9 build was compiled without any user-port RS-232 support at all, so none of the
2025-12-09 14:09:52 [kimi-k2-0905] `-rs232user*` switches exist.
2025-12-09 14:09:52 [kimi-k2-0905] You need a binary that was built with
2025-12-09 14:09:52 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-09 14:09:52 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-09 14:09:52 [kimi-k2-0905] --enable-rs232user
2025-12-09 14:09:52 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-09 14:09:52 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-09 14:09:52 [kimi-k2-0905] (or use the standard `-rs232dev` / `-rs232file` options that talk to the C64’s IEC-serial
2025-12-09 14:09:52 [kimi-k2-0905] bus instead of the user-port).
2025-12-09 14:09:52 [kimi-k2-0905] 
