2025-12-10 09:51:30 [nitro@ryzen5] how to enable vice socket connection?
2025-12-10 09:51:40 [kimi-k2-0905] VICE ≥ 3.7
2025-12-10 09:51:40 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 09:51:40 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Settings → RS-232 settings…
2025-12-10 09:51:40 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. “User-port RS-232 emulation” → ON
2025-12-10 09:51:40 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. “Device 4” (or the one you picked) → IP232
2025-12-10 09:51:40 [kimi-k2-0905] 4. Host: 127.0.0.1   Port: 25232
2025-12-10 09:51:40 [kimi-k2-0905] 5. OK → hard-reset the emulated C-64 (Alt-R or Reset button).
2025-12-10 09:51:40 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 09:51:40 [kimi-k2-0905] The socket is opened the moment the C-64 opens the RS-232 channel; no further switch is needed.
2025-12-10 09:51:40 [kimi-k2-0905] 
