2025-12-10 11:53:43 [kimi-k2-0905] "Device not present" means the C64 isn't seeing anything at device #4.
2025-12-10 11:53:43 [kimi-k2-0905] Check the chain:
2025-12-10 11:53:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 11:53:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Vice is set to "User-port RS-232" (not serial 1/2).
2025-12-10 11:53:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. The RS-232 device in Vice points to the real or virtual port your host is listening on.
2025-12-10 11:53:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. The host listener is actually running and bound to that same port (8081).
2025-12-10 11:53:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 4. No other process has the port open.
2025-12-10 11:53:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 5. Vice was restarted after any RS-232 setting change.
2025-12-10 11:53:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 11:53:43 [kimi-k2-0905] Once Vice recognises the interface the OPEN will succeed; until then the C64 will keep reporting
2025-12-10 11:53:43 [kimi-k2-0905] "device not present".
2025-12-10 11:53:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
