2025-12-10 20:19:03 [nitro@ryzen5] addressing modes of 6502
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 6502 addressing modes (13 total)
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Implied
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    `CLC`
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    No operand; the opcode itself tells the CPU what to operate on.
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Accumulator
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    `ASL A`
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    The operation is done on the A register; the operand letter “A” is only syntax sugar.
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. Immediate
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    `LDA #$55`
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    Operand byte is the actual value, not an address.
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 4. Zero-page
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    `LDA $55`
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    Operand is an 8-bit address in page 0 (0040–00FF).
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 5. Zero-page,X
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    `LDA $55,X`
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    Effective address = ($55 + X) & 0xFF (wraps inside page 0).
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 6. Zero-page,Y
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    `LDX $55,Y`
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    Same as above but only LDX and STX use Y in zero-page.
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 7. Absolute
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    `LDA $1234`
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    Full 16-bit address given in operand.
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 8. Absolute,X
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    `LDA $1234,X`
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    Effective address = $1234 + X (no page-wrap on the add).
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 9. Absolute,Y
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    `LDA $1234,Y`
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]    Same idea with Y.
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 10. (Indirect,X)  “pre-indexed”
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]     `LDA ($20,X)`
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]     Pointer address = ($20 + X) & 0xFF; actual address is read from that zero-page pair.
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 11. (Indirect),Y  “post-indexed”
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]     `LDA ($20),Y`
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]     Pointer is fetched from zero-page pair at 20/21; effective address = pointer + Y.
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 12. Relative
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]     `BNE $F0`
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]     Branch target = PC + 2 + signed 8-bit displacement (-128 … +127).
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 13. Absolute indirect  (JMP only)
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]     `JMP ($1234)`
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905]     16-bit target address is fetched from the given address and address+1.
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] Those 13 cover every legal instruction form on the NMOS 6502.
2025-12-10 20:19:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
