2025-12-17 19:47:57 [nitro@ryzen5] what is VREF pin in pico?
2025-12-17 19:48:04 [kimi-k2-0905] VREF is the ADC voltage-reference input.
2025-12-17 19:48:04 [kimi-k2-0905] Connect a clean, stable voltage here (1.8 V – 3.3 V) and the RP2040 will use it as the full-scale
2025-12-17 19:48:04 [kimi-k2-0905] value for its ADC instead of the default 3.3 V rail.
2025-12-17 19:48:04 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-17 19:48:38 [nitro@ryzen5] how fast can the adc go?
2025-12-17 19:48:42 [kimi-k2-0905] 500 kS/s shared across all inputs is the hard limit; you can read one pin at 500 k or four pins at
2025-12-17 19:48:42 [kimi-k2-0905] ~125 k each.
2025-12-17 19:48:42 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-17 19:48:56 [nitro@ryzen5] even at less than 12 bit?
2025-12-17 19:49:02 [kimi-k2-0905] Yes – the 500 kS/s ceiling is set by the SAR ADC clock and sample-hold time, not the output width.
2025-12-17 19:49:02 [kimi-k2-0905] Dropping to 8-bit or 4-bit still has to wait for the converter to finish, so the aggregate rate
2025-12-17 19:49:02 [kimi-k2-0905] stays the same.
2025-12-17 19:49:02 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-17 19:49:55 [nitro@ryzen5] so us sample ?
2025-12-17 19:49:57 [kimi-k2-0905] 2 µs minimum per sample.
2025-12-17 19:49:57 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-17 19:50:08 [nitro@ryzen5] what is pixel clock of PAL C64?
2025-12-17 19:50:12 [kimi-k2-0905] ≈ 8 MHz (8.1818 MHz exact, 16 MHz master ÷ 2).
2025-12-17 19:50:12 [kimi-k2-0905] 
