2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] • `PIOFSTATRXFULL_LSB` is a bit position in the read-only `FSTAT` register
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] that tells you which FIFO is full* for each state machine.
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] 
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] Register Layout (per PIO block):
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] 
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] FSTAT (32-bit read-only):
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] [31:24]  RXFULL[3:0]   ← SM3 RX FIFO full?
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] [23:16]  TXFULL[3:0]   ← SM3 TX FIFO full?
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] [15:12]  RXEMPTY[3:0]  ← SM3 RX FIFO empty?
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] [11:8]   TXEMPTY[3:0]  ← SM3 TX FIFO empty?
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] [7:0]    FLEVEL[3:0]   ← FIFO fill levels
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] 
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] 
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] • Constants (pico-sdk):*
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] 
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] #define PIO_FSTAT_RXFULL_LSB    8   // Bit 8 = SM0 RX full
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] #define PIO_FSTAT_TXFULL_LSB    4   // Bit 4 = SM0 TX full
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] #define PIO_FSTAT_RXEMPTY_LSB   12  // Bit 12 = SM0 RX empty
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] #define PIO_FSTAT_TXEMPTY_LSB   0   // Bit 0 = SM0 TX empty
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] 
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] 
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] Your usage:
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] 
2025-12-21 11:15:20 [grok-4-1] const io_ro_32 EmptyBit = (1u << (PIO_FSTAT_RXEMPTY_LSB + machineIndex));
