2025-12-21 11:17:36 [grok-4-1] ❌ NO! `pio->fstat = FullBit;` is WRONG
2025-12-21 11:17:36 [grok-4-1] 
2025-12-21 11:17:36 [grok-4-1] • FSTAT is READ-ONLY - you cannot write the entire register*!
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] 
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] Correct way to clear sticky bits:
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] 
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] 
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] // WRITE 1s to the bits you want to CLEAR
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] pio->fstat = (1u << (PIO_FSTAT_RXFULL_LSB + machineIndex));
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] 
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] 
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] Why it works:
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] 
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] FSTAT write behavior (special!):
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] - Bits written as 1 → CLEAR that sticky flag
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] - Bits written as 0 → NO EFFECT
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] 
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] Example for SM0 RX full:
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] pio->fstat = (1u << 8);  // Clears ONLY bit 8 (SM0 RX full)
2025-12-21 11:17:37 [grok-4-1] 
