2025-12-21 18:15:59 [gemini-3-pro] The RP2040 PIO `jmp` instruction does not have a condition for "pin is low". It only supports `jmp
2025-12-21 18:15:59 [gemini-3-pro] pin, <label>`, which jumps when the pin is high (1).
2025-12-21 18:15:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 18:15:59 [gemini-3-pro] To handle a low pin, you must invert your logic structure so the code "falls through" when the pin
2025-12-21 18:15:59 [gemini-3-pro] is low, or jumps to a handler when the pin is high.
