2025-12-21 22:01:49 [nitro@ryzen5] what is PIO_FSTAT_TXEMPTY_LSB in rp2040
2025-12-21 22:02:03 [gemini-3-pro] `PIOFSTATTXEMPTY_LSB` is a constant defined in the RP2040 C/C++ SDK hardware register
2025-12-21 22:02:03 [gemini-3-pro] headers. It represents the Least Significant Bit position (value 24) of the `TXEMPTY` field
2025-12-21 22:02:03 [gemini-3-pro] within the PIO's `FSTAT` (FIFO Status) register.
2025-12-21 22:02:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:02:03 [gemini-3-pro] This field contains four bits (bits 24 through 27), where each bit corresponds to one of the four
2025-12-21 22:02:03 [gemini-3-pro] State Machines in a PIO block. A value of `1` in the respective bit indicates that the Transmit
2025-12-21 22:02:03 [gemini-3-pro] FIFO for that State Machine is empty.
2025-12-21 22:02:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:03:58 [nitro@ryzen5] for c side what bit says it is ok to call pio_sm_get
2025-12-21 22:04:15 [gemini-3-pro] `PIOFSTATTXEMPTY_LSB` is a constant defined as 24. It represents the Least
2025-12-21 22:04:15 [gemini-3-pro] Significant Bit position of the `TXEMPTY` field within the PIO `FSTAT` (FIFO Status) register. This
2025-12-21 22:04:16 [gemini-3-pro] field contains 4 bits (one for each state machine) indicating if the Transmit FIFO is empty.
2025-12-21 22:04:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:04:16 [gemini-3-pro] To determine if it is okay to call `piosmget` (which reads from the RX FIFO), you check the
2025-12-21 22:04:16 [gemini-3-pro] `RXEMPTY` bit for the specific state machine in the `FSTAT` register.
2025-12-21 22:04:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:04:16 [gemini-3-pro] • Register Bit: `RXEMPTY` (located starting at `PIOFSTATRXEMPTY_LSB`, which is
2025-12-21 22:04:16 [gemini-3-pro] 8).
2025-12-21 22:04:16 [gemini-3-pro] • Condition: The bit must be 0 (cleared). If the bit is 1, the FIFO is empty and
2025-12-21 22:04:16 [gemini-3-pro] blocking reads will stall.
2025-12-21 22:04:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:11:28 [nitro@ryzen5] this version gets stuck, i was hoping to detect long and short low periods
2025-12-21 22:11:29 [nitro@ryzen5] .program luma2sync	mov	x, !nullloop0:		jmp	pin, isnotlow	jmp	islowisnotlow:	jmp	x--, loop0islow:	set	x, 31	mov	isr, !nullloop1:	jmp	pin, ishigh	jmp	x--, loop1	mov	isr, null	mov	x, !null	jmp	loop1ishigh:	push
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] • PIOFSTATTXEMPTY_LSB*
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] In the RP2040 `hardware/regs/pio.h`, `PIOFSTATTXEMPTY_LSB` is 24. It represents the
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] bit shift for the Transmit FIFO Empty flag in the `FSTAT` register.
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] • C Side Read Check*
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] To check if it is safe to call `piosmget` (meaning data is available), you need to check
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] that the RXEMPTY bit is 0.
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] In the C SDK, use the helper function:
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] if (!pio_sm_is_rx_fifo_empty(pio, sm)) {
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	uint32_t data = pio_sm_get(pio, sm);
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] }
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] If accessing the register directly, check the `PIOFSTATRXEMPTY_BITS` (Bit 8) of the `FSTAT`
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] register.
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] • Fixed PIO Code*
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] Your version likely gets stuck because it lacks a `.wrap` directive (falling off the end into
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] invalid memory) and `push` blocks if the C code isn't reading fast enough.
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] Here is a corrected version that detects if a low period is longer than 31 cycles.
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] // .program luma2sync
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] .wrap_target
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	wait 1 pin 0		; Wait for line to be High (ensure we catch an edge)
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	wait 0 pin 0		; Wait for falling edge (Start of low period)
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	set x, 31		; Set threshold counter
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	mov isr, !null		; Initialize ISR to All-Ones (indicates "Short")
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] measure_loop:
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	jmp pin, publish	; If pin goes high early, it was Short. Jump to push.
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	jmp x--, measure_loop	; Decrement X. If X is not 0, keep checking.
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	; Fallthrough: X hit 0. The pulse is Long.
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	mov isr, null		; Set ISR to 0 (indicates "Long")
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	wait 1 pin 0		; Wait for the pin to finally go high
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] publish:
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	push			; Push ISR to RX FIFO (Blocks if full)
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] .wrap
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] • Configuration Note:*
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] Ensure you configure the JUMP pin in your C setup, or `jmp pin` will not work:
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] void luma2sync_program_init(PIO pio, uint sm, uint offset, uint pin) {
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	pio_sm_config c = luma2sync_program_get_default_config(offset);
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	// Map the specific pin to the JMP PIN selector
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	sm_config_set_jmp_pin(&c, pin);
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	// Map the specific pin to the INPUT selector (for 'wait')
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	sm_config_set_in_pins(&c, pin);
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	pio_gpio_init(pio, pin);
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	pio_sm_init(pio, sm, offset, &c);
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] 	pio_sm_set_enabled(pio, sm, true);
2025-12-21 22:12:03 [gemini-3-pro] }
