2025-12-21 22:14:43 [nitro@ryzen5] will wait 0 default to pin 0?
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] PIOFSTATTXEMPTY_LSB
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] `PIOFSTATTXEMPTY_LSB` is defined as 24 in the RP2040 SDK. It represents the bit
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] position (Least Significant Bit) within the `FSTAT` register for the "Transmit FIFO Empty" flags.
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] C-Side RX Check
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] To determine if it is safe to call `piosmget` (meaning the RX FIFO is not empty),
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] you must check the RXEMPTY bit.
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] If the bit is 0, data is available.
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] bool is_rx_ready(PIO pio, uint sm) {
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 	// Check if the RXEMPTY bit for the specific state machine is 0
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 	return !(pio->fstat & (1u << (PIO_FSTAT_RXEMPTY_LSB + sm)));
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] }
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] Wait Instruction Syntax
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] No, `wait 0` does not default to pin 0. The syntax requires a source and an index.
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] • `wait 0 pin 0` waits for Pin 0 (mapped input) to be low.
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] • `wait 0 gpio 0` waits for absolute GPIO 0 to be low.
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] Corrected PIO Program
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] Your previous version likely got stuck due to the logic flow in `loop1` and how `x` was handled.
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] The following program detects low periods by counting down `x` while the pin is low, then pushes
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] the inverse of the counter (duration) to the FIFO.
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] .program luma2sync
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] ; Reusable function to measure low pulse duration
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] public measure_low_pulse:
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 	pull block          ; Optional: Stall until C side is ready (or remove if free-running)
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 	mov osr, null       ; Clear OSR
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 	out null, 32        ; Clear OSR shift counter if needed
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] wait_for_low:
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 	wait 0 pin 0        ; Wait for pin to go LOW
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] start_measurement:
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 	mov x, !null        ; Initialize X to 0xFFFFFFFF (-1)
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] count_loop:
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 	jmp pin, pulse_ended ; If pin goes HIGH, pulse is over
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 	jmp x--, count_loop  ; Decrement X and continue loop
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] pulse_ended:
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 	mov isr, x          ; Move remaining value of X to ISR
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 	push noblock        ; Push to RX FIFO
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 	jmp wait_for_low    ; Reset for next pulse
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] • C-Side Helper:*
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] uint32_t read_pulse_width(PIO pio, uint sm) {
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 	// 0xFFFFFFFF - value = number of cycles spent in low state
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] 	return 0xFFFFFFFF - pio_sm_get_blocking(pio, sm);
2025-12-21 22:15:09 [gemini-3-pro] }
