2025-12-21 22:34:30 [gemini-3-pro] To answer your specific configuration questions:
2025-12-21 22:34:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:34:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Jmp Pin*
2025-12-21 22:34:30 [gemini-3-pro] You need to use `smconfigsetjmppin` to define which specific GPIO the `jmp pin`
2025-12-21 22:34:30 [gemini-3-pro] instruction monitors.
2025-12-21 22:34:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:34:30 [gemini-3-pro] • In Shift and Auto Push*
2025-12-21 22:34:30 [gemini-3-pro] You do use `smconfigsetinshift` to manage the Input Shift Register (ISR). To turn
2025-12-21 22:34:30 [gemini-3-pro] auto push off, set the `autopush` parameter to `false` when calling this function.
2025-12-21 22:34:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:34:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Pin Directions*
2025-12-21 22:34:30 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, `piosmsetconsecutivepindirs` is necessary. You must explicitly configure the
2025-12-21 22:34:30 [gemini-3-pro] pins as inputs; otherwise, the state machine may read its own internal drive state rather than the
2025-12-21 22:34:30 [gemini-3-pro] external signal required for your `wait` and `jmp` instructions.
2025-12-21 22:34:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
