2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] To answer your specific configuration questions:
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] • 1. `setjmppin`???*
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, you must configure which pin the `jmp pin` instruction checks. Use the function
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] `smconfigsetjmppin` in your C setup code to map this specific instruction to a
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] GPIO.
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] • 2. Do I need `smconfigsetinshift`?*
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, it is highly recommended. Even if you don't use auto-push, you need this to define the shift
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] direction (Right or Left) for your `in` instructions so bits accumulate in the correct order.
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] • 3. How do I turn auto push off?*
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] You turn it off using the `smconfigsetinshift` function mentioned above. The third
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] parameter is a boolean for `autopush`; simply pass `false`.
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] • 4. Is `piosmsetconsecutivepindirs` necessary?*
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] Yes. While the PIO state machine can "read" a pin regardless of direction, this function configures
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] the electrical direction of the GPIO pads. If you do not set them to inputs, the PIO might read the
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] state of the internal output driver rather than the external signal.
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] • Observation on `luma2sample` and FIFO Join*
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] You mentioned using `PIOFIFOJOIN_RX` for the second program (`luma2sample`). This setting
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] merges the TX FIFO into the RX FIFO, leaving you with zero TX depth.
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] Because your program starts with `pull block`, the state machine will likely hang indefinitely. It
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] is waiting for data from the TX FIFO, but the CPU cannot write to it because it has been disabled
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] by the join. You should either remove the `pull block` instruction or remove the FIFO join if the
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] PIO needs to receive configuration data from the CPU.
2025-12-21 22:36:12 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] I have reviewed the provided PIO assembly and C++ initialization code. While the logic seems
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] structured for video signal capture, there are three specific issues regarding configuration
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] application and FIFO management that will likely prevent the code from functioning.
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Configuration Application Order
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro]     In `initLuma2`, `piosminit` is called before
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] `smconfigsetfifojoin`. The `piosminit` function loads the configuration
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] into the hardware registers. Modifying the `config` struct afterwards has no effect unless
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] `piosmset_config` is called again.
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  SyncIndex FIFO Direction
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro]     The `luma2sync` program ends with a `push` instruction, which writes to the RX FIFO. However,
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] the C++ configuration sets `PIOFIFOJOIN_TX` for this state machine. This merges the memory
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] into a large TX FIFO, leaving the RX FIFO with zero depth. The state machine will stall
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] indefinitely at the `push` instruction.
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  SampleIndex Trigger
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro]     The `luma2sample` program executes `pull block` at the start (after an initial push). This
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] instruction waits for the CPU to write data to the TX FIFO. The provided C++ code does not appear
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] to write to the `SampleIndex` state machine, meaning the sampling loop will never begin.
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] If you would like corrected code snippets for the initialization sequence, please let me know.
2025-12-21 22:45:11 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:48:11 [nitro@ryzen5] i want sample to pull data from sync fifo, is this possible?
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] No, it is not possible for one State Machine (SM) to pull directly from another SM's FIFO within
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] the PIO hardware itself. The FIFOs are connected to the system bus, not internally routed between
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] SMs.
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] To achieve this, you must use a DMA (Direct Memory Access) channel to bridge the two state
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] machines. The DMA will automatically read from the `Sync` RX FIFO and write to the `Sample` TX
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] FIFO.
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] Additionally, your `fifo_join` configuration in `main.cpp` is currently inverted, which will cause
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] the programs to stall.
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  `luma2sync` uses `push`, so it needs the RX FIFO (you disabled it by joining TX).
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  `luma2sample` uses `pull`, so it needs the TX FIFO (you disabled it by joining RX).
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the corrected configuration and the DMA bridge setup.
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] main.cpp
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] #include "hardware/dma.h"
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] // ... existing includes and vars ...
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] void initLuma2() {
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 	// --- SyncIndex Setup ---
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 	const pio_program_t *program1 = &luma2sync_program;
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 	uint offset1 = pio_add_program(pio, program1);
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 	config[SyncIndex] = luma2sync_program_get_default_config(offset1);
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 	pio_gpio_init(pio, 2);
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 	pio_sm_set_consecutive_pindirs(pio, SyncIndex, 2, 1, false);
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 	gpio_pull_up(2);
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 	sm_config_set_jmp_pin(&config[SyncIndex], 2);
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 	sm_config_set_in_pins(&config[SyncIndex], 2);
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 	sm_config_set_in_shift(&config[SyncIndex], true, false, 1);
2025-12-21 22:48:45 [gemini-3-pro] 
