2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] Here are a few observations regarding the provided PIO assembly and C++ integration.
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] PIO Program (`luma2sync`)
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  ISR Overwrite: In your `loop` and `ishigh` sections, you initialize the ISR using `mov
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] isr, !null` or `mov isr, null`. However, the subsequent `bitloop32` executes `in pins 1` exactly 32
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] times. Since the ISR is 32 bits wide, this loop will completely overwrite the initialization value
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] (0x00000000 or 0xFFFFFFFF) with new data from the pins before the `push` occurs. The initialization
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] instructions may be redundant.
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Pin Mapping: You are using `wait ... pin 0`. Ensure that
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] `smconfigsetinpins` maps the base pin correctly so that relative pin 0 corresponds
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] to your physical `SyncPin`.
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] C++ Code (`main.cpp`)
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  DMA vs. CPU Polling Conflict:
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro]     *   You initialize and configure a DMA channel to read from the PIO DREQ
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] (`piogetdreq`).
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro]     *   However, `readLuma2()` manually reads data using `piosmget(pio, SyncIndex)`.
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro]        Issue: If the DMA is enabled, it will automatically drain the RX FIFO. The CPU
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] call to `piosmget` will likely find the FIFO empty or race with the DMA, resulting in
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] missing data. You should choose either DMA or* CPU polling, not both.
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  DMA Configuration Errors:
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Missing Arguments: `dmachannelconfigure()` is called without arguments. It
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] requires `channel`, `config`, `writeaddr`, `readaddr`, `transfer_count`, and `trigger`.
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Write Increment: You have set `channelconfigsetwriteincrement(&c,
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] false)`. If you intend to fill `buffer` or `pixelBuffer`, this must be set to `true`. currently,
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] the DMA will overwrite the same memory address repeatedly.
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  PIO Configuration:
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Shift Threshold: `smconfigsetinshift` is set with a threshold of
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] `1`. While `autopush` is false, it is generally safer to set the threshold to `32` when shifting in
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] full 32-bit words, particularly if you ever switch to autopush.
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  Buffer Safety:
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro]     *   In `readLuma2`, `buffer[syncCount++&1023]=t;` uses a bitwise AND for ring buffering. Ensure
2025-12-21 23:05:21 [gemini-3-pro] `syncCount` does not overflow logic elsewhere if it is used as a linear counter.
