2025-12-21 23:24:58 [gemini-3-pro] No, you cannot instruct the PIO `in` instruction to use "base + 1". The `in pins` instruction
2025-12-21 23:24:58 [gemini-3-pro] always reads starting from the configured `in_base`.
2025-12-21 23:24:58 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 23:24:58 [gemini-3-pro] If you strictly keep `smconfigsetinpins(&config, SyncPin);` (Pin 2), your data
2025-12-21 23:24:58 [gemini-3-pro] sampler `in pins 1` will read Pin 2, not Pin 3.
2025-12-21 23:24:58 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 23:24:58 [gemini-3-pro] To sample Pin 3 (Data) while keeping Pin 2 (Sync) logic, you must shift the Input Base to
2025-12-21 23:24:58 [gemini-3-pro] Pin 3 in C++, and adjust the Wait instructions in PIO to look "backwards" (wrap around) to
2025-12-21 23:24:58 [gemini-3-pro] Pin 2.
