2025-12-21 23:36:46 [gemini-3-pro] To address your specific question about `base+1`: The PIO `in pins` instruction always reads
2025-12-21 23:36:46 [gemini-3-pro] starting from the base pin defined in the configuration. You cannot offset the `in` instruction
2025-12-21 23:36:46 [gemini-3-pro] itself (e.g., `in pins+1, 1`) without changing the configuration base.
2025-12-21 23:36:46 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 23:36:46 [gemini-3-pro] To read the Luma pin while checking the Sync pin, you should configure the JMP pin to
2025-12-21 23:36:46 [gemini-3-pro] `SyncPin` and the IN pins to `LumaPin`.
2025-12-21 23:36:46 [gemini-3-pro] 
