2025-12-21 23:57:07 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, you are currently getting an overflow because the DMA channel stops automatically after
2025-12-21 23:57:07 [gemini-3-pro] completing the specified transfer count (`11 * 240`), while your PIO program continues to push data
2025-12-21 23:57:07 [gemini-3-pro] into the FIFO.
2025-12-21 23:57:07 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 23:57:07 [gemini-3-pro] To fix this, you must configure a DMA interrupt to reset the write address and restart the channel
2025-12-21 23:57:07 [gemini-3-pro] immediately upon completion.
2025-12-21 23:57:07 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-21 23:57:07 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the updated implementation using a named interrupt handler function.
