2025-12-22 00:01:32 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, you must restart the DMA channel. The DMA controller stops automatically once it completes the
2025-12-22 00:01:32 [gemini-3-pro] configured transfer count (`11*240`), but your PIO program continues to push data, filling the
2025-12-22 00:01:32 [gemini-3-pro] FIFO.
2025-12-22 00:01:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-22 00:01:32 [gemini-3-pro] To achieve continuous transfer ("no overflow"), you should implement an interrupt handler to reset
2025-12-22 00:01:32 [gemini-3-pro] the write address and re-trigger the DMA immediately upon completion.
2025-12-22 00:01:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-22 00:01:32 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the named function for the interrupt handler and the required setup lines.
2025-12-22 00:01:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
