2025-12-30 15:44:13 [scudmarks@discord] the fit3 server crashes every few hours now, am still unsure if i want to inpsect logs
2025-12-30 15:44:17 [kimi-k2-0711] If it’s dying repeatedly, the quickest triage is:
2025-12-30 15:44:17 [kimi-k2-0711] 
2025-12-30 15:44:17 [kimi-k2-0711] 1. `journalctl -u <service>` (or `docker logs <container>`) to see the last 20 lines—usually the
2025-12-30 15:44:17 [kimi-k2-0711] fatal error is right there.
2025-12-30 15:44:17 [kimi-k2-0711] 2. If the crash is OOM, `dmesg -T | tail` will say “killed process … out of memory”.
2025-12-30 15:44:17 [kimi-k2-0711] 3. If it’s a panic/stack trace, note the top frame; that’s the place to patch.
2025-12-30 15:44:17 [kimi-k2-0711] 
2025-12-30 15:44:17 [kimi-k2-0711] Five-minute skim is usually enough to decide whether it’s a quick fix or “restart and ignore until
2025-12-30 15:44:17 [kimi-k2-0711] next year”.
2025-12-30 15:44:17 [kimi-k2-0711] 
2025-12-30 15:45:26 [scudmarks@discord] i am loathe to run it in debugger, more interesting tasks at hand
2025-12-30 15:45:28 [kimi-k2-0711] Fair call. Add `--restart unless-stopped` (or `systemd Restart=always`) and bump the log level to
2025-12-30 15:45:28 [kimi-k2-0711] ERROR only—gives you the crash line when you eventually feel like looking without drowning you in
2025-12-30 15:45:28 [kimi-k2-0711] noise.
